<td>Professional Major</td>\n    <td>Rewenable Energy Systems and Water Management</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Instructor(s)</td>\n    <td>Ismo Halonen, Senior Lecturer</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td colspan=\"2\">The aim of this thesis was to build a measuring instrument for on site measuring of turbidity in surface waters. The device should be portable, have a watertight housing and comply with the measuring principles described in the widely used ISO 7027-1:2016 measuring standard. In addition, the aim was to calibrate the device according to ISO 7027-1:2016.<br><br>The sensor housing and internal support structures were designed in SolidWorks and printed with a masked stereolithography (MSLA) 3D printer. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nACADEMICS – Alban Cobi Design & Engineering | Mechanical Engineering Services (https://albancobi.com/academics/)\nciteturn0search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.7 years ago; Crawled: last week; A dual-port, smartphone-linked, pocket-sizefluorimeter for rapid molecular diagnostic assays at ... Projects have included the laser seal, electric vehicles, light displays, and museum exhibits.\n\n## ACADEMICS\n\n## PUBLICATIONS (2012 – Present)\n\nA dual-port, smartphone-linked, pocket-size\nfluorimeter for rapid molecular diagnostic assays at\npoint-of-care, 2025 (Manuscript submitted for publication to IEEE)\n\n* * *\n\nMS Thesis: A Suction-Based Reversible Attachment and Locomotion Mechanism for an Underway Vessel Hull Cleaning and Inspection Robot, 2017-2020\n\n* * *\n\nDesign of a Reconfigurable Quality Assurance Phantom for Verifying the Spatial Accuracy of Radiosurgery Treatments for Multiple Brain Metastases, 2019\n\n* * *\n\nBS Thesis: Design of a Carbon Fiber Suspension System for FSAE Applications , 2011-2012\n\n* * *\n\n## TEACHING (1989 – Present)\n\nI am very passionate about the sharing of knowledge because if we’re going to solve some of the world’s problems we have to 